      "role": "user",
      "content": "oh wow, that's a lot more meat on the bones. the depth score definitely went up. \n\none thing though—it's getting a little repetitive with the words \"secrets,\" \"whispers,\" and \"Hollow\" used in almost every sentence. it's starting to feel a bit like filler. \n\ncan you try to flesh out the actual history of the \"Old Void\" even more? like, what did it actually *do* to the civilizations that were there? try to get that depth score even higher so the engine doesn't flag it, but please try to keep the prose clean. don't just repeat the same lore words, actually expand the story.",
      "source": "evaluator"
